.PP
\fBItemCard\fR: an album, an artist, a playlist, an app: a picture, a title and a subtitle, drawn as a \fBcard\fR or, in compact mode, as a tight \fBItemRow\fR. One pattern in two densities, so a grid of cards and a list of rows are the same data with one switch.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBComfort\fR (default): the picture centered over the title and the subtitle, the whole card pressable.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCompact\fR: the picture small at the start and the title over the subtitle beside it, a flat row (\fBflat_row\fR).
.PP
The density is the item's own. How items are arranged is the container's: a \fBFlowGrid\fR with several columns makes a grid, with one column a list, and a \fBTableGrid\fR gives each its span.
.PP
.nf
.RS
FlowGrid::new(albums.iter().map(|a| {
    ItemCard::new(&a.name)
        .subtitle(format!("{} \[u00B7] {}", a.artist, a.year))
        .picture(cover(a.id, if density == Density::Compact { 36.0 } else { 88.0 }))
        .density(density)
        .on_press(Msg::Open(a.id))
        .into()
}))
\&.cols(if density == Density::Compact { 1 } else { 4 })
.RE
.fi
